    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The first Persian Empire, built by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#cyrus-the-great">Cyrus the Great</a>, stretched from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#indus">Indus</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#aegean">Aegean</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#nile">Nile</a>.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#darius-i">Darius I</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#satrapy">satrapies</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#royal-road">Royal Road</a>, coinage and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#aramaic">Aramaic</a> chancery became the model for later Near Eastern empires.</li><li>Weakened by revolts and court murders, it fell to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> in just four years, 334 to 330 BCE.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Royal couriers on the 2,700-kilometre <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#royal-road">Royal Road</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#susa">Susa</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#sardis">Sardis</a> could cover the distance in around a week, using relays of fresh riders.</p></aside>
    </section>

