uers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#egypt">Egypt</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">480 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#xerxes-i">Xerxes</a> invades <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#greece">Greece</a>, wins at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#battle-of-thermopylae">Thermopylae</a>, sacks <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#athens">Athens</a> but loses at Salamis</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">404 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#egypt">Egypt</a> revolts on the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#darius-ii">Darius II</a> and stays independent for six decades</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">343 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#artaxerxes-iii">Artaxerxes III</a> reconquers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#egypt">Egypt</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">331 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> defeats <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#darius-iii">Darius III</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#battle-of-gaugamela">Gaugamela</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">330 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">Alexander burns <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#persepolis">Persepolis</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#darius-iii">Darius III</a> is murdered by his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#satrapy">satrap</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#bessus">Bessus</a></span></li></ol>
